            <ArticleTitle>[Bilateral catheter for continuous TAP block and postoperative pain relief after gynecologic surgery].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>67-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.annfar.2010.08.012</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe the case of two patients who had undergone gynecologic surgery and in whom a continuous ropivacaine infusion was administered through a catheter placed on each abdominal side, using the technique of ultrasound-guided TAP block. Postoperative analgesia was of excellent quality with almost no morphine requirement. No side effects were encountered.</AbstractText>
